      "writtenOn": "2024-12-20T16:51:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "side note: This check does not make any sense. enforceNetworkStackPermission calls Context#checkCallingOrSelfPermission() and checks whether this process or the calling process has NETWORK_STACK or MAINLINE_NETWORK_STACK permission.\n\nThis code runs in system server, so I believe checkSelfPermission() eventually runs ActivityManagerService#checkComponentPermission which grants all permissions to the system server uid.\n\nCheck calling permission is based on Binder.getCallingUid(), which in turn only works on the binder thread (it\u0027s based on the thread-local IPCThreadState). However, this code runs on the service-local handler thread..\n\nNote: This was added in aosp/1553695 but I cannot figure out why. Presumably a copy / paste error from looking at the other CLs in that topic.\n\n---\n\nBy the way, this would throw a SecurityException which would kill the handler thread as it is not caught by the surrounding try / catch. I believe this invokes the deafult UncaughtExceptionHandler set by RuntimeInit (KillApplicationHandler) and takes down system server.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/os/RuntimeInit.java;l\u003d245\n\n---\n\nUploaded aosp/3428919 to remove it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 592,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 592,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "3a342f16bcc15c3785f8a8c1b3f288af021b346f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
