      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T08:04:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI we found several similar inconsistencies with WiFi permissions when reimplementing WifiManager APIs in ARC.\n\n\u003e  permission is based on Binder.getCallingUid(), which in turn only works on the binder thread (it\u0027s based on the thread-local IPCThreadState). However, this code runs on the service-local handler thread..\n\nThe way thar we ve dealt with this in ARC code is to always do the permission checks in the class that actually implements the Binder stub and then delegate to the real impl. We could do something similar here and move all perm checks to EthernetServiceImpl.java. WDYT ?",
      "parentUuid": "b449104a_7c83b7f8",
