      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T08:04:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can happen for real if the interface is immediately removed by the kernel after being added: `addInterface` gets scheduled on the handler and by the time we do the RTM_GETLINK request, we get ENODEV in the rtnl response. Actually I would suggest dropping the log level to `w` here. On CrOS we have test that stress test the stack to add and remove eth links and we see this type of races quite a bit.",
      "parentUuid": "d9c6e6e6_23d2d804",
      "revId": "3a342f16bcc15c3785f8a8c1b3f288af021b346f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
