      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T21:34:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh right. We should actually already have the flags from the RTM_NEWLINK, we just don\u0027t propagate them. The other entry point calls NetworkInterface.getNetworkInterfaces(). There we could use NetworkInterface#getFlags which uses SIOCGIFFLAGS (though if there is reason to write the netlink code anyways, I am not against it).\n\nThis might require some refactoring because moving an interface in and out of tethering mode also calls addInterface(). Though if we properly kept track of the tethering interface\u0027s link state, then it would not have to.",
      "parentUuid": "20eea1d8_e41b1558",
      "revId": "3a342f16bcc15c3785f8a8c1b3f288af021b346f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
